# 🚀 AWS Console Troubleshooting: Credential Validation & API Error Fix

## 📌 Problem Statement

While accessing AWS EC2 Console, I encountered the following issues:

- ❌ API Error
- ❌ "AWS was not able to validate the provided access credentials"
- ❌ Console not loading properly

Even after:
- Re-login
- Changing browser
- Using different network

The issue persisted.

---

## 🔍 Root Cause Analysis

After systematic troubleshooting, I identified:

👉 The problem was caused by *Proxy Configuration (Use Setup Script enabled)* in Windows network settings.

This proxy was:
- Interfering with AWS secure authentication
- Modifying API requests
- Causing credential validation failure

---

## 🛠️ Troubleshooting Steps

### Step 1: Verified Account & AWS Status
- Checked AWS account functionality on another laptop ✅
- Confirmed issue was device-specific

---

### Step 2: Eliminated Common Causes
- Cleared browser cache
- Used Incognito mode
- Switched networks
- Flushed DNS (ipconfig /flushdns)

---

### Step 3: Identified Root Cause
- Found "Use setup script" enabled in proxy settings

---

### Step 4: Fix Applied

Disabled proxy settings:




Turned OFF:
- ❌ Use setup script  
- ❌ Use proxy server  

Turned ON:
- ✅ Automatically detect settings  

---

## ✅ Final Result

- AWS Console working properly ✔️  
- EC2 dashboard loading ✔️  
- No credential/API errors ✔️  

---

## 💡 Key Learnings

- Proxy settings can break cloud authentication
- Always compare behavior across devices
- System-level issues can mimic cloud/API failures
- Structured troubleshooting is critical

